consinit() calls simplefb_init_cons() unconditionally, so the kernel does
not link once the AWS config drops the framebuffer stack. Removing the call
costs nothing on EC2: Nitro arm64 instances have no framebuffer device and
the console is on the serial port anyway.

--- sys/arch/arm64/arm64/machdep.c
+++ sys/arch/arm64/arm64/machdep.c
@@ -205,7 +205,6 @@ consinit(void)
 	mvuart_init_cons();
 	pluart_init_cons();
 	qcuart_init_cons();
-	simplefb_init_cons(&arm64_bs_tag);
 }
 
 void
